      "text": "Since $150^\\circ$ is an interior angle of a triangle, we can draw a triangle with two sides of length 1 and an included angle of $150^\\circ$. Using the Law of Cosines, we have:\n\n\\[AC^2 = 1^2 + 1^2 - 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\cos 150^\\circ\\]\n\\[= 1 + 1 - 2 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\]\n\\[= 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\]\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, let $BC = AC = \\sqrt{2-\\sqrt{3}}$. Since $\\angle ABC = 120^\\circ$, we have $\\cos 120^\\circ = -\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTherefore,\n\\[ \\boxed{ \\cos 150^\\circ = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} } \\]",
